            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nAfter her death, Franklin's contributions to the discovery of DNA's structure gained wider acknowledgment. She is now regarded as a key figure in molecular biology and genetics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nFranklin died on April 16, 1958, from ovarian cancer. Her legacy endures in the scientific community, which continues to celebrate her life and work in the advancement of molecular biology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Inspiring Future Generations</strong><br>\nFranklin's story has inspired many, particularly women in science, to pursue research despite obstacles. Her dedication and achievements have paved the way for future generations of scientists.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
